 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you doing? That's a common problem. The eyes are often the first part people see, and they need to be balanced. It' not low, it' right. The bottom half of the face should be even with half way up the eyes. Keep the nose about the length of one eye. A bit of squiggle near nose often makes it look better. Enjoy it. Practice really does make a difference. How' your face looking in the morning?",
